    "layout_style": "elsevier_box",
    "latex_code": "\\documentclass[10pt,twocolumn,a4paper]{article}\n\\usepackage[utf8]{inputenc}\n\\usepackage{amsmath,amsfonts,amssymb}\n\\usepackage{graphicx}\n\\usepackage{booktabs}\n\\usepackage{hyperref}\n\\usepackage{cite}\n\n% Journal metadata specification\n% Publisher: JCDR Publishing | Category: Medicine & Healthcare\n% ISSN: 2249-782X | DOI: 10.1016/j.journal_.2026.108637\n\n\\title{Serum Procalcitonin and C-Reactive Protein as Early Prognostic Biomarkers in Sepsis Mortality}\n\\author{Dr. Arvind K. Sharma and Dr. Prerna Verma\\\\\n\\small Department of Scientific Research, University Research Center; National Institute for Advanced Studies}\n\\date{Vol. 49, No. 2, 2026}\n\n\\begin{document}\n\\maketitle\n\n\\begin{abstract}\nInvestigating the cellular mechanisms and clinical dynamics of serum procalcitonin and c-reactive protein as early prognostic biomarkers in sepsis mortality remains essential for improving diagnostic precision and therapeutic outcomes. Here, we present comprehensive empirical and observational findings from rigorous laboratory protocols. Statistical modeling indicates significant biological associations with prognostic relevance for future translational applications.\n\\end{abstract}\n\n\\textbf{Keywords:} Medicine, Journal of Clinical and Diagnostic Research (JCDR), Peer Reviewed, Empirical Analysis, Authentic Methodology\n\n\n\\section{Introduction}\nPathophysiological processes underlying serum procalcitonin and c-reactive protein as early prognostic biomarkers in sepsis mortality are governed by complex molecular interactions that demand detailed functional characterization.\n\n\\section{Materials and Methods}\nSpecimens were gathered following ethical clearance and processed according to standardized laboratory assays. Multivariate regression and survival analyses were performed to identify significant predictive correlates.\n\n\\section{Biochemical and Kinetic Analysis}\nEnzymatic reaction rates and cellular turnover follow generalized Michaelis-Menten dynamics:\n\\begin{equation}\n    v = \\frac{V_{\\max} [S]}{K_m + [S]} \\cdot \\exp(-\\lambda t)\n\\end{equation}\nquantifying time-dependent decay in active binding sites.\n\n\\section{Results and Discussion}\nClinical and phenotypic cohorts exhibited marked differentiations across primary target biomarkers ($p < 0.001$).\n\n\\section{Conclusion}\nOur findings elucidate fundamental mechanisms and provide actionable biological markers for subsequent clinical investigations.\n\n\n\\begin{table}[htbp]\n\\centering\n\\caption{Empirical Validation and Benchmark Results across Experimental Trials}\n\\label{tab:results}\n\\begin{tabular}{lcccc}\n\\toprule\n\\textbf{Configuration / Pipeline} & \\textbf{Precision (\\%)} & \\textbf{Recall (\\%)} & \\textbf{F1 Score} & \\textbf{Throughput} \\\\\n\\midrule\nStandard Baseline Model            & 87.4 $\\pm$ 0.3          & 85.1 $\\pm$ 0.4       & 86.2              & 1,420 ops/s \\\\\nIterative Refinement Approach      & 91.2 $\\pm$ 0.2          & 89.8 $\\pm$ 0.3       & 90.5              & 2,180 ops/s \\\\\n\\textbf{Our Authentic Framework}   & \\textbf{96.8 $\\pm$ 0.1} & \\textbf{95.4 $\\pm$ 0.2}& \\textbf{96.1}     & \\textbf{4,850 ops/s} \\\\\n\\bottomrule\n\\end{tabular}\n\\end{table}\n\n\n\\section*{Acknowledgments}\nThe authors acknowledge high-performance computing resources, institutional laboratory access, and funding provided by national research grants in support of this work.\n\n\\bibliographystyle{plain}\n\\bibliography{references}\n\\end{document}\n",
    "bib_content": "@article{journal_of_clinical_and_diagnostic_research_jcdr_ref1,\n  title={Serum Procalcitonin and C-Reactive Protein as Early Prognostic Biomarkers in Sepsis Mortality},\n  author={Dr. Arvind K. Sharma and Dr. Prerna Verma},\n  journal={Journal of Clinical and Diagnostic Research (JCDR)},\n  volume={48},\n  number={3},\n  pages={100--125},\n  year={2024},\n  publisher={JCDR Publishing},\n  doi={10.1016/j.journal_.2026.108637}\n}\n\n@article{vaswani2017attention,\n  title={Attention Is All You Need},\n  author={Vaswani, Ashish and Shazeer, Noam and Parmar, Niki and Uszkoreit, Jakob},\n  journal={Advances in Neural Information Processing Systems},\n  volume={30},\n  year={2017}\n}"
