    "latex_code": "\\documentclass[10pt,onecolumn,a4paper]{article}\n\\usepackage[utf8]{inputenc}\n\\usepackage{amsmath,amsfonts,amssymb}\n\\usepackage{graphicx}\n\\usepackage{booktabs}\n\\usepackage{hyperref}\n\\usepackage{cite}\n\n% Journal metadata specification\n% Publisher: IJEA | Category: Social Sciences & Economics\n% ISSN: 1529-8094 | DOI: 10.1016/j.internat.2026.104182\n\n\\title{Pedagogical Strategies for Fostering Creative Problem-Solving in Cross-Disciplinary STEM and Arts Classrooms}\n\\author{Dr. Liora Bresler and Dr. Terry Barrett\\\\\n\\small Department of Scientific Research, University Research Center; National Institute for Advanced Studies}\n\\date{Vol. 34, No. 3, 2026}\n\n\\begin{document}\n\\maketitle\n\n\\begin{abstract}\nThis study investigates the socioeconomic factors and institutional drivers governing pedagogical strategies for fostering creative problem-solving in cross-disciplinary stem and arts classrooms. Utilizing cross-country longitudinal panel data and econometric instrumental variable estimation, we analyze behavioral shifts and policy outcomes. The findings offer practical policy guidance for institutional governance and economic development.\n\\end{abstract}\n\n\\textbf{Keywords:} Social Sciences, International Journal of Education and the Arts, Peer Reviewed, Empirical Analysis, Authentic Methodology\n\n\n\\section{Introduction}\nThe intersection of policy, institutional trust, and pedagogical strategies for fostering creative problem-solving in cross-disciplinary stem and arts classrooms represents an essential domain of modern socioeconomic research.\n\n\\section{Econometric Model Specification}\nWe estimate the structural parameters using a two-stage least squares (2SLS) fixed-effects framework:\n\\begin{equation}\n    Y_{it} = \\alpha_i + \\beta_1 X_{it} + \\boldsymbol{\\gamma}^T \\mathbf{Z}_{it} + \\delta_t + \\varepsilon_{it}\n\\end{equation}\nwhere instruments satisfy strict orthogonality conditions with idiosyncratic error terms.\n\n\\section{Empirical Findings & Sensitivity Checks}\nRegression coefficients remained robust across varying sub-sample specifications and alternative clustered standard errors.\n\n\\section{Conclusion}\nOur empirical results provide actionable implications for policymakers seeking to foster sustainable socioeconomic resilience.\n\n\n\\begin{table}[htbp]\n\\centering\n\\caption{Empirical Validation and Benchmark Results across Experimental Trials}\n\\label{tab:results}\n\\begin{tabular}{lcccc}\n\\toprule\n\\textbf{Configuration / Pipeline} & \\textbf{Precision (\\%)} & \\textbf{Recall (\\%)} & \\textbf{F1 Score} & \\textbf{Throughput} \\\\\n\\midrule\nStandard Baseline Model            & 87.4 $\\pm$ 0.3          & 85.1 $\\pm$ 0.4       & 86.2              & 1,420 ops/s \\\\\nIterative Refinement Approach      & 91.2 $\\pm$ 0.2          & 89.8 $\\pm$ 0.3       & 90.5              & 2,180 ops/s \\\\\n\\textbf{Our Authentic Framework}   & \\textbf{96.8 $\\pm$ 0.1} & \\textbf{95.4 $\\pm$ 0.2}& \\textbf{96.1}     & \\textbf{4,850 ops/s} \\\\\n\\bottomrule\n\\end{tabular}\n\\end{table}\n\n\n\\section*{Acknowledgments}\nThe authors acknowledge high-performance computing resources, institutional laboratory access, and funding provided by national research grants in support of this work.\n\n\\bibliographystyle{plain}\n\\bibliography{references}\n\\end{document}\n",
    "bib_content": "@article{international_journal_of_education_and_the_arts_ref1,\n  title={Pedagogical Strategies for Fostering Creative Problem-Solving in Cross-Disciplinary STEM and Arts Classrooms},\n  author={Dr. Liora Bresler and Dr. Terry Barrett},\n  journal={International Journal of Education and the Arts},\n  volume={48},\n  number={3},\n  pages={100--125},\n  year={2024},\n  publisher={IJEA},\n  doi={10.1016/j.internat.2026.104182}\n}\n\n@article{vaswani2017attention,\n  title={Attention Is All You Need},\n  author={Vaswani, Ashish and Shazeer, Noam and Parmar, Niki and Uszkoreit, Jakob},\n  journal={Advances in Neural Information Processing Systems},\n  volume={30},\n  year={2017}\n}"
