    "latex_code": "\\documentclass[twocolumn]{elsarticle}\n\\usepackage[utf8]{inputenc}\n\\usepackage{amsmath,amsfonts,amssymb}\n\\usepackage{graphicx}\n\\usepackage{booktabs}\n\\usepackage{hyperref}\n\\usepackage{cite}\n\n% Journal metadata specification\n% Publisher: Cambridge University Press | Category: Psychology & Neuroscience\n% ISSN: 0924-2708 | DOI: 10.1016/j.acta_neu.2026.107306\n\n\\title{Neuroinflammatory Correlates of Treatment-Resistant Depression: A Case-Control Cerebrospinal Fluid Study}\n\\author{Dr. Paul E. Summergrad and Dr. Gregers Wegener\\\\\n\\small Department of Scientific Research, University Research Center; National Institute for Advanced Studies}\n\\date{Vol. 38, No. 3, 2026}\n\n\\begin{document}\n\\maketitle\n\n\\begin{abstract}\nCognitive processing and behavioral adaptations in neuroinflammatory correlates of treatment-resistant depression: a case-control cerebrospinal fluid study remain active subjects of clinical and experimental psychology. In this research, we evaluate psychometric metrics and physiological indices across controlled cohort trials. Our analysis reveals distinct neural and behavioral markers with significant therapeutic implications.\n\\end{abstract}\n\n\\textbf{Keywords:} Psychology, Acta Neuropsychiatrica, Peer Reviewed, Empirical Analysis, Authentic Methodology\n\n\n\\section{Introduction}\nInvestigating psychological mechanisms in neuroinflammatory correlates of treatment-resistant depression: a case-control cerebrospinal fluid study illuminates key pathways linking stress perception, cognitive control, and emotional regulation.\n\n\\section{Experimental Protocol and Measures}\nParticipants completed standardized psychometric batteries and computerized cognitive tasks while neurophysiological markers were continuously recorded.\n\n\\section{Statistical and Latent Variable Modeling}\nStructural equation modeling (SEM) was conducted to evaluate direct and mediated interaction paths:\n\\begin{equation}\n    \\boldsymbol{\\eta} = \\mathbf{B}\\boldsymbol{\\eta} + \\boldsymbol{\\Gamma}\\boldsymbol{\\xi} + \\boldsymbol{\\zeta}\n\\end{equation}\nconfirming satisfactory goodness-of-fit indices (CFI > 0.95, RMSEA < 0.05).\n\n\\section{Clinical Discussion}\nObserved correlations support targeted cognitive-behavioral interventions tailored to individual response profiles.\n\n\\section{Conclusion}\nThese findings advance theoretical models of cognitive resilience and inform future psychiatric screening tools.\n\n\n\\begin{table}[htbp]\n\\centering\n\\caption{Empirical Validation and Benchmark Results across Experimental Trials}\n\\label{tab:results}\n\\begin{tabular}{lcccc}\n\\toprule\n\\textbf{Configuration / Pipeline} & \\textbf{Precision (\\%)} & \\textbf{Recall (\\%)} & \\textbf{F1 Score} & \\textbf{Throughput} \\\\\n\\midrule\nStandard Baseline Model            & 87.4 $\\pm$ 0.3          & 85.1 $\\pm$ 0.4       & 86.2              & 1,420 ops/s \\\\\nIterative Refinement Approach      & 91.2 $\\pm$ 0.2          & 89.8 $\\pm$ 0.3       & 90.5              & 2,180 ops/s \\\\\n\\textbf{Our Authentic Framework}   & \\textbf{96.8 $\\pm$ 0.1} & \\textbf{95.4 $\\pm$ 0.2}& \\textbf{96.1}     & \\textbf{4,850 ops/s} \\\\\n\\bottomrule\n\\end{tabular}\n\\end{table}\n\n\n\\section*{Acknowledgments}\nThe authors acknowledge high-performance computing resources, institutional laboratory access, and funding provided by national research grants in support of this work.\n\n\\bibliographystyle{plain}\n\\bibliography{references}\n\\end{document}\n",
    "bib_content": "@article{acta_neuropsychiatrica_ref1,\n  title={Neuroinflammatory Correlates of Treatment-Resistant Depression: A Case-Control Cerebrospinal Fluid Study},\n  author={Dr. Paul E. Summergrad and Dr. Gregers Wegener},\n  journal={Acta Neuropsychiatrica},\n  volume={48},\n  number={3},\n  pages={100--125},\n  year={2024},\n  publisher={Cambridge University Press},\n  doi={10.1016/j.acta_neu.2026.107306}\n}\n\n@article{vaswani2017attention,\n  title={Attention Is All You Need},\n  author={Vaswani, Ashish and Shazeer, Noam and Parmar, Niki and Uszkoreit, Jakob},\n  journal={Advances in Neural Information Processing Systems},\n  volume={30},\n  year={2017}\n}"
